{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1554924993,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0MzE2NzcxOTU=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3316","origin":"github"},"title":"All \"committing\" commands should have -m|--message argument","message":"My use case currently:\n```shell\ndatalad create -d . -m \"Dataset with additionally preprocessed files\" preproc\n```\nin which case ideally we should commit in super dataset the addition of the newly created subdataset with that message.  Messages for commits within preproc should be \"automated\" ones I guess (thus possibly relates to #3236 (automated commit messages)) but I would not even mind if the last one (currently \"[DATALAD] new dataset\") would be the one I have provided.\n\nFor such multi-commit executions I even wonder if solution could/should be similar, or may be even the same in implementation, to #3265 (`run` to cover multiple commits).  The idea of the \"merge\" commit to depict the end of the single action  kinda make sense in such scenarios.  In `create` it is a bit tricky (start from an \"empty state commit\") but doable AFAIK.\n\nSimilarly  `install` which is in the case of installing a new subdatset (e.g. `install -d . URL`) would generate commit within super dataset.\n\nP.S. I though we had such an issue filed but couldn't find it. May be we discussed and closed already ;-)","files":null}]}